;
; key_multi_adorn_witness (K1, RP-10) -- the flagless multi-store flagship:
; the demand_multi_adorn_witness bf/fb graph with `@key(A) @key(B)` and NO
; `.drflags`. The two @key pragmas SELECT N=2 disjoint keyed stores flaglessly
; (RP-9 fallback), one pub, and answer identically to the flat/mono twin.
;
; K6-4 note (ADJ-K6-B): the pragma-FREE redeclaration below (FIRST, before the
; key-bearing decl) is the F-K6-SHADOW guard shape. Post-fix (ADJ-K6-A(b), the
; resolve-through-redeclarations accessors) it inherits the sibling's key
; SILENTLY (IDENTICAL-OR-ABSENT, absent arm) and compiles BYTE-IDENTICAL to the
; single-decl form; pre-fix it silently dropped the pragma
; (kSubgraphInstantiate 2 to 0), flipping every golden: the loud-regression
; guard. It hits the non-empty short-circuit, so it never reaches
; SameKeySetOfSets (that TRUE branch is exercised by reject_key_redecl_1).
#message edge_2(u64 A, u64 B).
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B).                 ; absent redecl - inherits @key silently
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B) @key(A) @key(B).
rel(A, B) : edge_2(A, B).
#query q(bound u64 A, free u64 B).
#query q(free u64 A, bound u64 B).
q(A, B) : rel(A, B).
